																		A Deconstruction of the Foundations Modus Operandi (SCP)
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/harvoable" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7005588); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=7005588&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607480085" alt="Harvoable " style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=7005588)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/harvoable" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7005588); return false;" >Harvoable </a></span> <span class="odate time_1607464341 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">08 Dec 2020 21:52</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4840022">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Horror, history, Foundation politics</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> Classic SCP layout; addenda will include a neutralisation proposal, interview with site-director, and a containment breach. This addenda will be presented in a novel style in the form an official document/folder (for an idea, see <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5859" target="_blank">SCP-5859</a>.)</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> The Foundation hears reports of people becoming infected with a seemingly untreatable strain of the Bubonic Plague. MTF Beta-7 (&quot;Maz Hatters&quot;) are deployed to control the situation. What follows is a deconstruction of the Foundations M.O: Secure, Contain, Protect.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">►&nbsp;Additional&nbsp;details</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">▼&nbsp;Additional&nbsp;details</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> The SCP in question is a the corpse of a 14th century Parisian male discovered deep within the catacombs of Paris (stumbled upon by Patient-Zero, an overeager urban explorer). Due to the anti-Semitic slur scorched into the corpse's chest, Foundation historians have theorised that the corpse was murdered due to the Christian persecution of the Jewish populace admist the onset of the Bubonic Plague.</p>
<p>The corpse is the cause of the outbreak. Exposure results in infection from an anomalous strain of <em>Yersinia pestis</em>. Initial stages of infection operate much the same way as a non-anomalous strain. However, rather than dying, the later stages of the anomalous strain cause those who are infected to lose higher cognitive brain function, who are then compelled to spread the disease.</p>
<p>Once the SCP is secured, the plot follows the project lead, Dr. Stephen Miller, in a vain attempt to neutralise the corpse due to the inherent risk of an XK-Class scenario if a containment breach were to occur. Unfortunately, his proposal is denied. He's given the usual spiel about how its a safe class object, how he'd be more at home at the Global Occult Coalition, about how historically attempted neutralisation of objects has often made things worse, which is why the Foundation contains rather than Destroy, Destroy, Destroy. The Site Director cites <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1609" target="_blank">SCP-1609</a> as an example; it was a teleporting chair that the GOC put through a wood chipper. Now, it's a murderous pile of splinters.</p>
<p>What follows is a breach. An area of Site-19 becomes infected, and Beta-7 are deployed to clean up the mess, resulting in the death of Miller.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> We discover that SCP-1609 (and many others) are completely fabricated. <em>They don't exist</em>. They are nothing but Foundation propaganda, a way to convince Foundation personnel that the GOC are incompetent and the Foundations way is the correct way&#8230; the <em>only</em> way, to deal with the anomalous. Moreover, they serve as a warning to those who would try to preemptively neutralise an anomalous object. The breach was orchestrated by the O5s to kill Miller after discovering the secret.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> Rough draft available on request.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

