					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/jack-howitzer" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7075879); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=7075879&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607480085" alt="Jack Howitzer" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=7075879)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/jack-howitzer" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7075879); return false;" >Jack Howitzer</a></span> <span class="odate time_1607469758 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">08 Dec 2020 23:22</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4840079">
									

<p>The O5's at it again, eh? I do like the idea of the Council doing shady shit - has a lot of potential and is supremely logical. You've got some issues though.</p>
<p>For a start, your SCP object. It's a generic zombie plague, and on top of that, the idea is already done by <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-008">SCP-008</a></p>
<p>I'd also like to ask you a few questions.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>1) How exactly does Miller find out about the conspiracy? Everything in the Foundation is under lock, key and blast gate when it comes to any sort of administration - let alone the O5.<br />
2) Why kill Miller ala FBI/FSB if they can just amnesticize him or change his memories? It's simple, quiet and cheap. More so than staging a breach is, at any rate.<br />
3) How are you planning to convey the whole story? I'm assuming you're going to write a different format after the article - no way is O5 letting a story like <em>that</em> be featured in one.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Frankly, I don't think it's even necessary for you to write an SCP if this story is all you'll be focusing on - you could just write it in as a tale around 1609. But then again, that's completely up to you.</p>
<p>Overall I think you have a great, great concept, but you just need to polish everything up and make it make sense in the end.<br />
It's a challenge!</p>

							</div>

								
