			<div class="content" id="post-content-4840129">
									

<p>Well, you obviously know your SCP. Better than I do, anyway. If there are any inconsistencies with the Foundationverse, I'm definitely not expert enough to identify them.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I still have something to say about the bacteria, though. I like the backstory and the fancy microbiology I barely grasp, however:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>&#8230;later stages of the anomalous strain cause those who are infected to lose higher cognitive brain function, who are then compelled to spread the disease.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>That's textbook zombies. The nuances you've added to the bacteria's mechanism don't really change it in that regard - the outcome is still bad meat with no brains.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>&#8230;the infected aren't undead or anything; they'll die just as easy as any other human.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The T-Virus zombies from RE are also technically alive and are also just deprived of high brain functions. Not less textbook zombie for it.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<br />
That's the only part I'm having trouble digesting. But aside from that, looks good to me. Then again, me also knows jack shit about top clearance levels, XK-Scenarios and all that jazz, so you gotta get that critted from someone else.
<p>Good luck!</p>

